VERSION: 2.0 (2026-10-12)  2.0 = merged set of 11 patches (old numbers below)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0005)

Document zoom and sidebar size (was 0010 v1.0):
- Document zoom 50-200%: Ctrl+wheel and pinch (anchored at the pointer),
  Ctrl/Cmd + = - 0 by event.code (Persian layout works). View-only, never
  saved; another document, leaving the page or a reload returns to 100%.
- CSS zoom on the document's Main column (--kms-doc-zoom); print is always
  100%; mobile unchanged. Badge with the zoom percent at the inline-end top,
  hidden at 100% and in print; click resets.
- Editor menus (toolbars, block menu, suggestions, find & replace) portal
  into a counter-zoomed host and scale with the document.
- Settings > Preferences "Sidebar size" 80-150%, saved as the interfaceZoom
  user preference (API: number 0.8-1.5); desktop only.

Right-click menu for the document area (was 0011 v1.0):
- Right-click on the title or body (read and edit mode) opens a document
  menu built on the action system; policies hide or disable items.
  Shift+right-click keeps the browser menu; mobile keeps the native
  long-press; ContextMenu key / Shift+F10 open it at the caret.
- Groups: clicked table/image/code block; selection (cut, copy, copy as
  Markdown / plain text, paste, paste as plain text, comment, link); new
  document / sub-document / from template; Insert; links and share; find &
  replace, table of contents, full width, text direction, zoom; AI (disabled,
  "Coming soon"); export and print; history, star, pin, move, duplicate,
  template, archive, delete; log out.
- Read-only and shared views offer only copy, link, view and export items.
- The menu scales with the document zoom (Menu primitives accept a portal
  container); DocumentZoom exposes zoom in / out / reset.

